**1.** A liquid-crystal video display comprising:

a liquid-crystal display panel having a plurality of image regions;

a backlight assembly positioned behind the liquid-crystal display panel and comprising a plurality of light-source substrates, each light-source substrate carrying a plurality of light-emitting diodes configured to illuminate a respective one of the image regions;

a controller configured to receive video data for presentation by the liquid-crystal display panel, determine a local brightness value for each of the image regions based on a corresponding portion of the video data, and generate control data for independently controlling the light-emitting diodes of the respective light-source substrates according to the determined local brightness values; and

a daisy-chain communication path connecting the light-source substrates in series with the controller, each light-source substrate being configured to receive the control data through a preceding light-source substrate or the controller, extract control data addressed to that light-source substrate, control its light-emitting diodes based on the extracted control data, and forward at least a portion of the control data to a succeeding light-source substrate.
